# Security-sensitive paths require review from a maintainer familiar with
# the trust model (see docs/security/threat-model.md and SECURITY.md).
# GitHub only enforces this as a required check if branch protection on
# `master` requires review from code owners — see SECURITY.md for the
# settings this repo asks maintainers to enable.

/internal/extension/    @nokhodian
/internal/secrets/      @nokhodian
/internal/chromecookies/ @nokhodian
/chrome-extension/      @nokhodian
/.github/workflows/     @nokhodian
/.mcp.json              @nokhodian

# Release signing path: the workflow, the signing tool, the verifier and its pinned keys, the
# guard scripts and the runbook. Whoever can change these can change what gets signed.
/.github/                        @nokhodian
/cmd/release-manifest/           @nokhodian
/internal/release/               @nokhodian
/scripts/check-release-tags*.sh  @nokhodian
/scripts/release-flatten.sh      @nokhodian
/docs/release-runbook.md         @nokhodian
